      "prompt": "Two sensors share a mounting bracket that vibrates, so a large part of their errors is common. A designer fuses them as independent. What is the consequence?",
      "kind": "choice",
      "dimension": "C",
      "critical": true,
      "options": [
        "The stated variance is smaller than the true error variance (overconfidence)",
        "The fused estimate becomes biased, because the common vibration shifts its mean",
        "Nothing, as long as both sensors have the same variance as each other",
        "The stated variance is larger than the truth, so the filter is too cautious"
      ],
      "answer": "0",
      "explanation": "Common error does not average out, but the independent formula assumes it does.",
